@startuml launch
title M-UM2: launch and authorised stop (v0 design; nothing implemented)

participant "swarma-dispatcher\n(service account swarma-dispatcher)" as D
participant "sudo\n(trusted root transition)" as S
participant "swarma-user-launcher\n(root, no arguments)" as L
database "Policy, ledger, lock, journal, audit, receipts\n(root-owned control state)" as R
participant "curator-run -> harness\n(agent worker-dev-7f3, UID/GID 30412 example)" as E
participant "swarma-credential-broker\n(its service account; owns credentials/bindings/leases)" as B
participant "swarma-user-manager\n(root, no arguments)" as M

note over D,M
  [[../spec/helper.md#7-the-launcher-swarma-user-launcher Defining spec §7 launcher]],
  [[../spec/helper.md#47-execstop §4.7 stop]], [[../spec/helper.md#5-cross-component-reconciliation §5 effect IDs]].
  Current repository: unimplemented design; v0 installs static range deny; v1 narrows egress/admission, v2 grants (§13).
  SH2+ joint admission remains gated by I4 publication (§14); dispatcher is the only launcher caller.
  Executor intake / Decision 0021 amendment is publication work (§7), not implemented here.
  Manager owns ledger/journal/audit; launcher writes root-owned start receipts.
  Agent owns home content; broker owns credentials/bindings/leases; dispatcher owns execution lifetime.
end note
note over L,R
  R-START / I4: session host requests dispatcher host_start; no privileged host call.
  R-SESSION: host admission permit is session-scoped for one logical_session_id.
  Successors require session lifecycle authorisation (member unpublished),
  previous claim confirmed absent and idempotency per (logical_session_id, op_id).
  Each physical start keeps (execution_id, controller_epoch, op_id) claim/fence/receipt.
  host_stop: session-host principal only, execution under permit, journaled E-stop;
  host-requested, distinct from owner cancel; no start authority.
  Fence change withdraws/reconciles permit; cancel before call prevents launch.
  Ambiguous call uses SAME effect/receipt; stop if required, never a second launch.
  Runner opens fresh authenticated host channel; current-epoch registration/readiness
  before delivery. Host failure retains claim and closed fence until reconciliation.
  Joint authentication/permit/crash/readiness publication remains open (§14 question 3).
  These values add no fields to launch-op/1; no helper host role or host sudo authority.
end note
D -> S: sudo /opt/swarma/libexec/swarma-user-launcher\n(stdin: swarma-user-manager launch-op/1)
note over D, L: Schema sketch: v:1, op:launch.start, request_id:launch effect ID,\ngeneration:9ac67d3418e04b0aafe89c6d72b54103, execution_id, epoch, executor:curator-run, plan\nRequest <= 80 KiB; plan <= 64 KiB base64 / 48 KiB decoded; stdin within 5 s
S -> L: exec as root (SUDO_UID = dispatcher)
break Invalid invocation, closed schema, bounds, role or grants in v0/v1 (§§2-3)
  L --> D: refuse; no launch
end
L -> L: scrub untrusted inherited FDs > 2 FIRST; keep caller-owned 0-2\nthen reserve read-only FD3 without clobbering internal handles
L -> R: shared transition lock; validate integrity, UID reservations, accounting;\nrecover only operation dependencies within budget (§4.6)
note over L,R: Compare OS objects with journal: dependency recovery: create rolls back; stop/retire continue.\nRetain generation lock through root receipt and completed verified UID/GID drop (R-FD3).
L -> R: 9ac67d3418e04b0aafe89c6d72b54103 active, kind agent (workplace only after separate gate), caller owner?
break Inactive / retiring generation or wrong owner
  L --> D: generation_not_active / target_not_owned
end
L -> R: under generation lock: check persisted all-stop mark;\nrefuse ALL physical starts, including in-flight/workspace executors
L -> R: verify machine-selected pinned exec-profile identity and body digest;\npolicy drift refuses, retry/recovery retain pin
note over L,R: Before new physical start: zero UID processes; no unresolved prior execution/stop.
L -> R: recorded admission class and qualified host capability matrix;\nexec profile + ceiling/network/socket/deployment gates before start
L -> L: Linux root-created non-delegated per-execution unit;\nmacOS qualified sandbox / process-CPU limits / scheduling / quota / watcher
note over L,E: R-EXEC: OS allowlist; writable areas non-executable; no heavy/network tools.\nComplete invocation: fixed entrypoint/args/environment and transitive code/config inputs.\nShared executables only through qualified wrapper, no direct/indirect heavy bypass; no account-started loop.\nWorkplace ZERO egress: Linux no-external-interface namespace + Unix-only families;\nmacOS deny-network sandbox + per-UID deny; no subscription binding/lease or local harness.
L -> R: executor id → approved path + SHA-256
L -> L: open executable no-follow; verify digest; retain verified handle THROUGH exec
break Unapproved executor or digest mismatch
  L --> D: executor_not_approved / executable_digest_mismatch
end
L -> L: open agent home without following links as cwd
break Invalid home
  L --> D: cwd_invalid
end
L -> L: home as cwd; close directory handle at last use
L -> L: completely stage bounded immutable admitted plan on read-only FD3;
L -> L: fixed bootstrap environment; staging and pre-exec path bounded
break Interrupted / failed / unknown staging
  L -> L: release internal handles and staging resources; preserve journal evidence
  L --> D: no launch; unknown cleanup is not absence
end
note over L,R
  R-FD3 (§7) owns the single descriptor lifecycle; agent launcher §10.1 references it.
  Per-platform staging/deadline/close-on-exec mechanism open (§14 question 7).
  Pipe allowed only with qualified capacity/feeder/deadline/cleanup order;
  never wait for a reader unable to start; no path/stdin/network fallback.
  EVERY failure branch releases internal handles/staging resources at safe last use,
  retains durable effect/receipt evidence and never infers absence from failed cleanup.
end note
L -> R: check for existing execution_id start receipt
break Receipt already exists
  L --> D: execution_already_started; no second start
end
L -> L: setsid
L -> R: atomic root-owned start receipt BEFORE privilege drop\nexecution_id, epoch, pid, start_time, boot_id, session_id; mode 0644
note over L,R: Keep lock and executable handle; close receipt/journal handles at last use.\nReceipt/effect evidence retained through reconciliation; exact bounds open (§14 question 8).
L -> L: clear supplementary groups; set GID, UID;\nverify root cannot be regained
break Privilege drop fails
  L -> L: release internal handles / staging resources; preserve receipt for reconciliation
  L --> D: privilege_drop_failed; no permission for another start
end
L -> L: after verified receipt-matching UID/GID transition: release and close generation lock
L -> E: exec verified executor as uid 30412; retain executable handle through kernel exec\ninternal handles close at last use or qualified close-on-exec\nexecutor receives only 0-2 and read-only FD3
note over L,E: Exec failure: release handles/staging resources; preserve receipt/effect evidence.\nUnknown outcome reconciles SAME effect; never launches twice (§§4.6, 7).
E -> E: verify immutable caller-composed plan and digested PATH;\nresolve protected credential binding (no profile composition)
note over D,E: Task resources read-only next to workspace, digests in plan; data, never instructions.\nTrusted side gathers/checks/attaches, including remote signed-letter attachments.\nMore requested by letter/outcome; worker never fetches; formats/caps unpublished (§8).\nWeb default-off; explicit per-identity trusted-circle opt-in only; no default search/fetch/donor web server.\nDefault donor loop reaches provider endpoints and our host; our side has no internet.\nLocal web-tool service owns account/row/listener; Unix socket + peer UID + grant only; workplaces refused.\nDonor web service separate from harness/bridge; key never reaches project (§8).
E -> B: trusted harness executor only; fresh connection; lease.request (broker lease-at-launch)
note over E,B: Lease refusal/recovery details unspecified in this spec §7; broker contract owns them.\nExecutor prepares work/ and tmp/ as agent UID, then execs harness; no profile composition.
note over S, E: Dispatcher owns the execution lifetime; sudo is never a signal relay
note over D,S
  NOPASSWD is confined to dispatcher helper/launcher rules (§2).
  swarma-operator and swarma-observer are protected services; neither hosts a harness or invokes launcher.
  Operator helper sudo requires authentication and timestamp_timeout=0 (§§2-3, 11).
end note

== Authorised stop (helper specification §4.7) ==
D -> S: sudo /opt/swarma/libexec/swarma-user-manager\n(stdin: swarma-user-manager helper-op/1, exec.stop)
note over D, M: Schema sketch: v:1, op:exec.stop, request_id:stop effect ID,\nargs:{generation:9ac67d3418e04b0aafe89c6d72b54103, execution_id, grace_seconds:10}; request <= 16 KiB\nStop and launch use distinct effect IDs; each retry reuses its own ID
S -> M: exec as root (SUDO_UID = dispatcher)
M -> R: shared lock; integrity/accounting and bounded dependency recovery
break Terminal stop result exists
  M --> D: replay result + current state WITHOUT signalling, including after successor
end
M -> R: unfinished/new stop: active caller-owned generation; LATEST start receipt
M -> M: pending continues same effect ID and ALL canonical arguments
M -> M: receipt authenticates target, never bounds process set;
M -> M: verify current generation/latest receipt and any live root identity
note over M,R: Absent root requires authoritative evidence; failed read is not absent.
break Receipt / generation mismatch or reused identity
  M --> D: refuse signalling (§4.7)
end
M -> M: stop per-user service domain where available
M -> E: TERM EVERY current-generation UID process; same grace; KILL remaining
M -> M: re-enumerate/revalidate identities; verify ZERO UID processes over quiet period
note over M,E: Same scope as retirement: escaped sessions, OS and pre-receipt processes included.\nNo wall-clock start-time filter; old receipt never signals a later execution.
alt Absence confirmed
  M --> D: stop receipt, remaining:0
else Processes remain
  M --> D: processes_remain; R-OUTCOME pending; continue same effect ID/args
else Observation unknown or failed
  M --> D: no success receipt; admitted work pending; caller cannot infer absence
  note over M,D: Exact observation-error code: unspecified in spec §4.7.
end
note over M,E
  exec.stop proves process absence ONLY; no harness native-lock absence (§4.7).
  Before reopen/resume, host recovery requires a fresh runner under agent UID
  to check the native lock under a closed fence and report to the host.
  Unknown native-lock result keeps session parked (session-host §3.5).
end note
note over D,E
  R-FATE table owned by §7 beside R-FD3: fate follows qualified kill domains, not setsid.
  Supervisor backend: daemon loss -> lost and journaled stop; no live adoption.
  SH2+ survival across controller-only restart requires qualified separate containment.
  Every old-daemon supervisor write is fenced by durable daemon-instance epoch.
  A service swap confirms absence for every affected execution; unit configs unpublished.
  R-TRANSFER: approved swarma-workspace-materialize before work;
  swarma-workspace-export after confirmed UID absence and workplace write fence.
  Child UID / fixed environment; no general launcher copy operation.
  Fresh standalone repository: no hooks/remotes/credential helpers; no linked cross-account worktree.
  Export recorded BEFORE retirement or explicit operator waiver; dispatcher owns obligation.
  OS profile blocks harness/agent binaries except admitted plan executor path.
  R-STANDING: trusted harness surfaces checked before launch/restart/native resume; drift refuses.
  R-VERIFY: builds/tests/worker-produced code only in secret-free off-host ephemeral runners.
  R-NETBIND: no direct/external-http-proxy binding for ANY platform account class.
  One profile-bound listener per bound account generation; only its own proxy.port admitted.
  N15 account_generation/profile_ref/service_generation/served_policy_digest evidence (§8).
  Operator trusted-circle admission enables donor-side opt-ins only; host boundaries stay.
end note
note over D,M
  R-WATCH v0: journaled account stop + published hold + observer status; no phone promise.
  Generation/boot/interval-bound samples; stale/unknown never retargeted.
  Per-account freeze lifecycle remains v1/S2 open (§8.2).
  R-ALLSTOP: manual operator authentication + one confirmation; refused inside agent sessions.
  Direct same-act fan-out; promptly issue range deny/broker freeze/host closure.
  Root receiver mark fences create/activation/launch/ingress BEFORE inventory.
  Stops progress without dispatcher or containment replies; operator helper path is narrowing only.
  Never-launched: full no-launch coverage + fresh generation-bound absence, no dummy receipt.
  Ambiguous/lost history stays unresolved; receipt-backed stops retain latest-receipt checks;
  broker freezes leases/renewals (delivered tokens keep vendor lifetime);
  host closes delivery/snapshots boards; every part journaled.
  Partial/unknown -> incident and closed admission; ALL service parts, dispatcher included,
  reconcile before explicit stopped-set/session-scope recovery; hold last, no restart (§8.3).
end note
@enduml
